60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Candidate D, the Mobile Branch, avoids the supplier delays. It uses our existing vehicle.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, but the running lines overran. Is the vehicle reliable enough?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle is already there. The risk is staffing, not equipment.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the grant covers session fees. The mobile service fits that model.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, the mobile service reaches the outer wards. That solves the bus link problem.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, yes! It brings the library to them. No more long trips.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, but what about the supervision? Who runs the help desk?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, we can use the retired tradespeople from the volunteer register.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, they are volunteers, not staff. The grant doesn’t cover their time.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, but the attendance is high. It’s worth the risk.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, the grant covers the contracted sessions. The mobile service is a contracted session.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, that’s a stretch. The grant is for specific fees, not general operations.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, but the endowment covers capital. The vehicle is capital.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the endowment is for one-off items. The running costs are ongoing.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, but the running lines overran. We need to be careful.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I think D is the best choice. It reaches the people who need us most.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m hesitant. The funding is risky. But the past shows we need to try.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,I agree with Yumi. The staffing gap is manageable. The impact is high.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. The grant covers the initial cost. We can manage the rest.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. The mobile service is the only option that reaches the outer wards.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
